What each is
- PlanterRun_2/4/Corner/End_<A|B|C>, PlanterArc: the original id. Every LOD is the adopted stonework (faces, normals, UVs, stone slots, same order: checked face by face against the adopted FBX, stone.json) + one testbed planting level. The dome slots (DK_Leaf_Civic(Dark), DK_Bloom_*, DK_Leaf_CoreShrub, DK_Leaf_Shrub, DK_Flower_Coral, DK_GroundCover) are gone; DK_Soil_TB, DK_Leaf_TB, DK_Petal_TB follow the stone slots. Levels: L0 inspection, L1 close, L2 near, L3 gameplay (PlanterArc: L0 close, L1 near, L2 gameplay).
- CafeTerrace, CafeUpper_3, CafeUpper_4, RecordsTower: the original id, its own LOD files and switch points (RecordsTower keeps lodClass landmark). Each level is the adopted level with the dome faces and slots removed; the stonework is unchanged. The planting is the companion <id>_Planting, placed at the parent's transform (same pivot and frame) with the four testbed levels. Why a companion: a 23-35 m LODGroup's own size would put the leaf-scale switch heights above 1.
- CivicBedPlanting_<bed> (5): the testbed's bed-level planting of each tufted civic bed. Pivot = the world ring's centroid at the kerb base, yaw 0, base 0.18 (row `placement`: at, world bed id, ring fit < 1 mm).
- GlobeLamp_TB: the testbed's globe lamp, one level (chrome housing DK_Chrome + opal globe DK_Opal_TB), no light baked in. Placement: one per PlanterArc at the row's arc-frame offset.
- Soil at run joints fixed: open-ended runs (all PlanterRun pieces, the terrace and crown troughs) take their soil flush with the open ends and inset on the side walls only, so neighbouring pieces' soil meets (check render out/scratch/vela/077/f/final-runs-runs-close-y210-auto.png).

LOD heights
- Per piece, from its own size (the largest bounds side): screen = size x px-per-m / 1080, at the testbed's switch points (café recipe 180 / 80 / 45 px per m; fountain 80 / 43.6). PlanterRun_4: 0.667 / 0.296 / 0.167, as derived. The 2, Corner and End pieces and PlanterArc are smaller, so their heights are lower (listed above). At play zoom (orthographic 14) every piece draws its gameplay level; close cameras get full detail.
- Companions and civic beds carry lodSize 4.0 with 0.667 / 0.296 / 0.167. That switches at orthographic half-height 3 / 6.75 / 12, the same leaf-scale rule whatever the group's extent.
- Per-piece values are better than one shared set: a single 0.667 / 0.296 / 0.167 on a 2 m piece would hold it at near or close at play zoom.

